    "title": "NI 45-106 s. 7.1 — Exemption (discretionary relief)",
    "content": "Section 7.1 — Exemption (discretionary relief)\n\n7.1 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the regulator or the securities regulatory authority may grant an exemption to this Instrument, in whole or in part, subject to such conditions or restrictions as may be imposed in the exemption. (2) In Ontario, only the regulator may grant an exemption and only from Part 6, in whole or in part, subject to such conditions or restrictions as may be imposed in the exemption.\n\n(3) Except in Alberta and Ontario, an exemption referred to in subsection (1) is granted under the statute referred to in Appendix B of National Instrument 14-101 Definitions opposite the name of the local jurisdiction.\n\nCross-references: Part 6.\n\nSource: NI 45-106 unofficial consolidation current to 2025-12-04.",
